 "caution": "2.4 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 59,170 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages. Almost all of the Magahi text comes from literary blogs and short stories collected by the K.M. Institute, so the vocabulary leans towards written, literary Magahi. Spelling is not standardised; have a speaker check your items. Speakers of Magahi also know Hindi, and the two share much vocabulary. Every word form of Hindi (80,074 forms) was added to the reject list, so no pseudoword is a real Hindi word, and the app pre-selects Hindi under \"Exclude real words of other languages\" (the Word-in column shows near misses). Of the 59,170 reference words, 16,694 are also Hindi words; they stay in the lexicon because they are words of both languages. Magahi (Devanagari) is an abugida: CV (orthographic) counts every consonant letter as C plus an inherent vowel V unless a vowel sign or virama follows. CV (phonological) applies the Hindi-type schwa-deletion rule (not checked against pronunciations). Length is counted in aksharas.",
 "caution_items": [
  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "2.4 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 59,170 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Mostly one kind of text",
   "text": "Almost all of the Magahi text comes from literary blogs and short stories collected by the K.M. Institute, so the vocabulary leans towards written, literary Magahi. Spelling is not standardised; have a speaker check your items."
  },
  {
   "title": "Hindi words excluded",
   "text": "Speakers of Magahi also know Hindi, and the two share much vocabulary. Every word form of Hindi (80,074 forms) was added to the reject list, so no pseudoword is a real Hindi word, and the app pre-selects Hindi under \"Exclude real words of other languages\" (the Word-in column shows near misses). Of the 59,170 reference words, 16,694 are also Hindi words; they stay in the lexicon because they are words of both languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abugida: CV and length",
   "text": "Magahi (Devanagari) is an abugida: CV (orthographic) counts every consonant letter as C plus an inherent vowel V unless a vowel sign or virama follows. CV (phonological) applies the Hindi-type schwa-deletion rule (not checked against pronunciations). Length is counted in aksharas."
  }
 ],
